pleted":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in: 4.5.beta [c81fd6c51233a727da528cf7f74137d56b5d6efe]\n- Not reproducible in: 4.4.1.stable\n\n### System information\n\nmacOS\n\n### Issue description\n\nI've only had this issue reported to me by a client, but never seen it myself, so the description here is going to be a bit vague, but...\n\nIt seems there's been some regression between 4.4 and 4.5 that causes an error to be emitted randomly when saving GDScript files using the built-in script editor, saying:\n\n```\nERROR: Can't update documentation for \"[...]\".\n```\n\n... where `[...]` would be the class name (presumably if it's using `class_name`) or the script path.\n\nThe error itself was changed in #108418 from the previous `ERR_FAIL_COND(!EditorHelp::has_doc(p_name))` to provide more context. Unfortunately the class names/paths shown in the new error don't seem to have much in common that would indicate what the issue might be.\n\nThis error seems to show up only about once per day on average, so it's fairly rare, but frequent enough to be annoying. Re-saving the same file right afterwards does **not** seem to reproduce the error, which is unlike what's been reported in #108418, where @KoBeWi mentions it showing up on every save once the error does appear.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nNone yet, unfortunately.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNone yet, unfortunately.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}"